      "line": null,
      "code": "tokenizer_mode *the_current_tok = TOK_NEXT_MODE(tok);",
      "note": "In the vulnerable tree `tok_new()` initializes `tok->tok_mode_stack_index = 0` and the destination array is `tokenizer_mode tok_mode_stack[MAXLEVEL];` with `MAXLEVEL = 200`, so valid indexes are 0 through 199. The first-NUL-truncated witness contains 222 `f'{` starts and zero `}` bytes, so before the crashing start it can accumulate 199 active nested f-string modes without a pop. This line's `TOK_NEXT_MODE(tok)` expansion preincrements the index to 200 and yields a one-past-end pointer. The patch inserts `if (tok->tok_mode_stack_index + 1 >= MAXFSTRINGLEVEL) { return MAKE_TOKEN(syntaxerror(tok, \"too many nested f-strings\")); }` immediately before this line and resizes the stack to `MAXFSTRINGLEVEL`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
